   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## WEB4 Klein: style frame (full-page mood mockup)\nA picture of what a finished page *feels* like: colour, type weight, imagery, density, shape language. It is a **mood image, not a layout**: Front-end builds the real page. Label it that way on boards.\n\n- **Portrait** 9:16 or 2:3 = a long scrolling page (default 9:16, 1.5 MP). **Landscape** 16:9 or 3:2 = a desktop viewport above the fold.\n- Describe the page top to bottom: nav bar, hero (with its image), sections, cards, footer. Name the palette with hex-like words, corner radius, borders, shadow, spacing.\n- Klein will invent fake lettering. Ask for *text shown only as soft grey placeholder lines*, and never use a style frame where readable text matters.\n- To build the frame around a direction's real hero art, use WEB2 with the hero as `<ref_image_0>`.\n- Full model, 30 steps, CFG 3.5 (~35 s)."
   ]
  },
